menu "Opus codec (esp_opus_float)"

config OPUS_FIXED_POINT
    bool "Build Opus in fixed-point arithmetic"
    default n
    help
        Compile the Opus codec with -DFIXED_POINT: the CELT decoder uses
        integer arithmetic and the SILK fixed-point encoder sources are built.

        This is the prerequisite for ESP32-P4 PIE acceleration, whose SIMD is
        integer-only (no float vector instructions). It changes the decoded
        PCM bit-for-bit versus the float path, so validate fixed output
        against the fixed C reference (not the float hash).

        Default off keeps the float decode path and the OPUS_P4_KERNELS_FLOAT
        anti-collapse kernel unchanged.

config OPUS_P4_COMB_PIE
    bool "Use the ESP32-P4 PIE comb filter (fixed-point)"
    default n
    depends on OPUS_FIXED_POINT && IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
    help
        Route comb_filter_const_c through the PIE kernel opus_p4_comb8 (16x32
        via vmul.s32.s16xs16, unaligned taps via src.q). ~2x faster than scalar
        on the comb filter; relaxed (not bit-exact, ~-64 dB vs the C reference,
        within opus_compare tolerance). Misaligned buffers fall back to C.

endmenu
